    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d204">

                <pb facs="0160" n="152" sameAs="frus:frus1939v05/pg152"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">715.1715/1388: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Representative of the President</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Corrigan</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Panama</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-01-27T16:00:00-05:00">January 27, 1939—4
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 6:47 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>11. Referring to the Department’s telegram No. 7, January 24, 6 p.m., Dr.
                    Rodríguez after consultation with his Government states that he will be unable
                    to leave Bogotá to come to Panama at this time owing to the delicate status of
                    negotiations which he is conducting with the Colombian Government or to visit
                    the disputant countries “even should it be determined that it is advisable”.</p>
                <p>I shall confer with the Costa Rican member on his arrival here and communicate
                    his views to the Department.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Corrigan</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
